    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band faq" aria-labelledby="faq-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Questions</span><h2 id="faq-h">Fair questions.</h2>
    <details><summary>Does Kept prescribe or sell medication?</summary><p>No. Kept works alongside whoever prescribes for you — your doctor, a telehealth service or a specialist. We don’t sell drugs, compounded or otherwise.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Which medicines does it support?</summary><p>Zepbound and Mounjaro (tirzepatide), Wegovy and Ozempic (semaglutide), the Wegovy pill, Foundayo (orforglipron) and Saxenda (liraglutide). Each has its own dose ladder and missed-dose rules in the app.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Why so much about protein and muscle?</summary><p>Because the scale doesn’t show what you’re losing. Without enough protein and resistance training, a large share of GLP-1 weight loss can be muscle — and muscle is what protects strength, metabolism and the result after treatment.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What if I want to stop?</summary><p>That’s a conversation for you and your prescriber; Kept helps you plan it — maintenance dose, taper or stop — with daily habit targets and a guardrail that flags early regain.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is my health data safe?</summary><p>Your data is encrypted, never sold, never used for ads, and deletable at any time. If your employer sponsors Kept, they see only de-identified totals for groups of 10 or more.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band alt" id="waitlist" aria-labelledby="wl-h">
